{% import "github-repo-button.njk" as repo %}
{% import "stack-list.njk" as stack %}

<div class="prose">
  <p>Each piece has its own repository and lifecycle, and together they serve the Shellui frontend. The graph draws every Shellui service and how they connect.</p>
</div>

<section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="run-it-yourself">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="run-it-yourself">Run it yourself</h2>
    <p>Shellui is open source under the MIT license. The shell, the services, and the admin live in public repositories on <a href="https://github.com/shellui">GitHub</a>.</p>
    <p>Each service ships as a ready-made Docker image, so you can host identity, storage, hosting, and email on your own servers. The shell, admin, and file manager are static files you can serve from any host. <a href="{{ site.docs }}/backend/">Read the backend services docs</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">{% include "oss-visual-responsive.njk" %}</div>
</section>

<section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="map-the-stack">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="map-the-stack">Map the stack</h2>
    <p>Follow one box at a time. Pointing at a box or tabbing to it highlights what that box talks to, and each box title links to its section further down. Every arrow is also written out under the graph.</p>
  </div>
  {% include "architecture-graph.njk" %}
</section>

<div class="prose mt-16">
  {{ stack.heading("shellui", "Frontend", "shell") }}
  <p>The frontend lives in the shellui monorepo, a TypeScript React runtime. <code>@shellui/core</code> owns navigation, layout modes, themes, i18n, modals, and drawers. <code>@shellui/sdk</code> lets apps in iframes talk to the shell. <code>@shellui/cli</code> scaffolds and serves projects. Any stack can run inside the Shellui iframe.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["TypeScript", "React", "React Router", "shadcn", "Tailwind", "Workbox", "Roarr", "Sentry"]) }}
  <p>{{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/shellui") }}</p>

  {{ stack.heading("identity-service", "Backend", "identity-service") }}
  <p>The authentication backend is identity-service, a Django API. It covers 15 OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect providers, Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML) 2.0, and magic links. It issues JSON Web Token (JWT) sessions and publishes a JSON Web Key Set (JWKS).</p>
  <p>It ships as a Docker image.</p>
  <p>The image runs its scheduler itself, so webhook retries and data retention do not need cron. It also publishes metrics in Prometheus format.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["Python", "Django", "django-allauth", "Django REST Framework", "Swagger", "ReDoc"]) }}
  <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    {{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/identity-service") }}
    {{ repo.dockerImageButton("shellui/identity-service") }}
  </p>

  {{ stack.heading("admin", "Frontend", "admin") }}
  <p>The admin panel is a Vite + React app embedded in the shell at <code>/admin</code>. It manages users, company access, and operational data, and it reads the same identity-service as sign-in. It ships as static files.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["TypeScript", "React", "React Router", "shadcn", "Tailwind"]) }}
  <p>{{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/admin") }}</p>

  {{ stack.heading("storage-service", "Backend", "storage-service") }}
  <p>The storage-service is a Django API with a Storage REST API at <code>/storage/v1/*</code>. It verifies identity-service JWTs and writes blobs to S3 or the local filesystem. It ships as a Docker image.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["Python", "Django", "Django REST Framework", "django-storages", "Swagger", "ReDoc"]) }}
  <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    {{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/storage-service") }}
    {{ repo.dockerImageButton("shellui/storage-service") }}
  </p>

  {{ stack.heading("files", "Frontend", "files") }}
  <p>Files is a React file manager app. Set <code>filesUrl</code> and it handles browsing, upload, download, folders, permissions, and share links against storage-service. On the full stack it also embeds in the admin iframe. It ships as static files.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["TypeScript", "React", "React Router", "shadcn", "Tailwind"]) }}
  <p>{{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/files") }}</p>

  {{ stack.heading("hosting-service", "All-in temporary deploy", "hosting-service") }}
  <p>The hosting-service is a Django API that deploys the whole Browser group as static files - the shell, your app, and Files - under one temporary URL. It ships as a Docker image in your infrastructure. Use it while you try the product.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["Python", "Django", "Django REST Framework", "django-storages", "Swagger", "ReDoc"]) }}
  <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    {{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/hosting-service") }}
    {{ repo.dockerImageButton("shellui/hosting-service") }}
  </p>

  {{ stack.heading("email-service", "Backend", "email-service") }}
  <p>email-service is a Django API that sends Shellui mail. identity-service, storage-service, and hosting-service call it when <code>EMAIL_SERVICE_API_KEY</code> is set. An event applies that company's email rules. identity-service can also send sign-in mail directly.</p>
  <p>The company brings its own provider: Resend, Amazon SES, or SMTP. Sign-in mail always goes out first, so a newsletter or broadcast never delays it.</p>
  <p>It ships as a Docker image. The admin app manages rules, templates, and the provider. You can run the same image yourself.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["Python", "Django", "Django REST Framework", "Celery", "React Email", "Swagger", "ReDoc"]) }}
  <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    {{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/email-service") }}
    {{ repo.dockerImageButton("shellui/email-service") }}
  </p>
</div>
